{"author":{"id":"ce771b8a9b8c30a8aac165a8b1cdb0957637d3941276ec4f27335daee16d79de"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1794855286,"nonce":"bhWm3X1YuTPoHCNFIPB6w3dsS8Y=","title":"Spec: Light Cycle stepped bands and ECharts chart overhaul","was":"The grow overview's history charts are hard to read and hard to trust. They have no axes, no units, no time labels, and no hover feedback — only two faint corner numbers whose meaning is unclear. The shaded Target Band uses one range for the whole Chart window, so daytime readings sit \"out of range\" against night targets and vice versa: the band ignores whether the grow lights are on. One chart (humidity at the 30-day window) renders almost empty due to a band-maths bug, another shows a physically meaningless negative VPD, cards for sensors that aren't bound waste the whole page, and a stray soil-band form floats at the bottom of the grow page looking like leftover debug text."}]}